For your information, and based on your idea and Ilmen's idea, I added a 3=
=20
step processing:

   1. Clean the input in a generic way : tabs/spaces, split entries with=20
   spaces, etc. (see the sed script at this point=20
   <https://github.com/Sukender/lojban-spell-check/blob/2e93ceb/wordlist/cl=
ean.sed>,=20
   or its latest version=20
   <https://github.com/Sukender/lojban-spell-check/blob/master/wordlist/cle=
an.sed>
   )
   2. Clean from a "Lojbanic" point of view : remove non-lojban entries,=20
   prepend dot before words starting with vowels, etc. (current script=20
   <https://github.com/Sukender/lojban-spell-check/blob/2e93ceb/wordlist/cl=
ean_lojban.sed>=20
   / latest version=20
   <https://github.com/Sukender/lojban-spell-check/blob/master/wordlist/cle=
an_lojban.sed>
   )
   3. Split entries: cmevla, cmavo, compound cmavo, and a few other classes=
=20
   (current script=20
   <https://github.com/Sukender/lojban-spell-check/blob/2e93ceb/wordlist/sp=
lit.sed>
    / latest version=20
   <https://github.com/Sukender/lojban-spell-check/blob/master/wordlist/spl=
it.sed>
   )
  =20
Current results are:
38 "illegal" words, and 430 duplicates (mainly generated by splitting, such=
=20
as when processing "lo nu", "lo", "nu")

